completed_at: "2026-08-14T12:57:41.426Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "When a gate verdict is truncated, the retained assertion rows are ranked so that every assertion whose verdict is not pass appears before any assertion that passed, and a blocking verdict always ships with the rows that caused it; The verdict envelope emits the total assertion count evaluated alongside the rows retained, so a reader can compute what fraction of the evidence is present without a second invocation; The verdict envelope participates in the declared pagination contract rather than omitting its keys, so the absence of a continuation is stated rather than implied; A regression test evaluates a gate whose only failing assertion is declared last, reads the verdict at the default budget, and asserts the failing row is present in the retained set; The retention rule is declared as data on the surface rather than implied by row order, so a reader can tell which selection policy produced the retained subset"
parent: pm-1jzupz
risk: high
confidence: 90
resolution: fixed
expected_result: A truncated verdict retains every non-passing cause before passing evidence and states the full evaluated denominator and retention policy.
actual_result: "Assurance prioritizes all non-passing assertions, preserves their enforcement order, reports assertions_total and verdict_priority, and exposes bounded continuation for withheld evidence."
